--- a/source/medicationrequest/medicationrequest-introduction.xml
+++ b/source/medicationrequest/medicationrequest-introduction.xml
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
     <p>This resource would not be used when ordering a device(s) that may have a medication coating e.g. heparin coated stints, or similar types of devices. These types of devices would be ordered using the <a href="devicerequest.html">DeviceRequest</a> or the SupplyRequest resources.</p>
     <p>It is not intended for use in prescribing particular diets, or for ordering non-medication-related items (eyeglasses, supplies, etc.).  In addition, the MedicationRequest may be used to report orders/request from external systems that have been reported for informational purposes and are not authoritative and are not expected to be acted upon (e.g. dispensed or administered).
 </p>
-    <p>The MedicationRequest resource is a "request" resource from a FHIR workflow perspective - see <a href="workflow.html#request">Workflow Request.</a></p>
+    <p>The MedicationRequest resource is a "request" resource from a FHIR workflow perspective - see <a href="workflow.html#request">Workflow Request</a> – it serves as an authorization, which doesn't make it necessarily actionable, unless it has the 'actionable' tag set, or used in combination with a Task resource or in specific workflows - more information on the <a href="workflow-management.html">workflow pages</a>.</p>
 
 
 <p>
